{"t":1378617.9315784,"req":"h01","event":"done","status":"answered","level":0,"steps":["classify","retrieve","loop","draft"],"answer":"The original attention mechanism divides the query\u2011key dot products by a constant (specifically \\(1/\\sqrt{d_k}\\)) before applying softmax to prevent the dot products from becoming too large in magnitude when the dimensionality \\(d_k\\) is large. Large dot products push the softmax into regions with extremely small gradients, so scaling keeps the values in a range where the softmax is more stable and gradients are not vanishing [C:attention:10]."}
